ath: lift NO_IR from a country IE on cards programmed with a country

A card whose EEPROM holds a country code (the Pro1X's WCN3990: 0x80fa,
France) gets ath's custom world regulatory domain at registration, with
NO_IR on every 5 GHz channel.  cfg80211 clears NO_IR from beacon hints
only while world roaming, and a country IE ends that; ath's notifier
ignores the country IE for such cards.  So while a station was
associated, no AP could start on any 5 GHz channel, even the station's
own: iw phy showed 5180, 5745 and 5765 MHz "no IR" with wlan0 on 149 and
not 8 s after disconnecting (2026-11-20), and an AP beside it on 149
never left config.  Apply the beaconing flags for a country IE on these
cards too: NO_IR goes where the country's rules allow, radar
frequencies excepted.

Not upstream; the pro1x channel's.
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c
@@ -542,7 +542,21 @@
 			ath_reg_dyn_country(wiphy, reg, request);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_REGDOM_SET_BY_COUNTRY_IE:
-		ath_reg_dyn_country(wiphy, reg, request);
+		/*
+		 * A card programmed with a country keeps its regulatory domain,
+		 * but its channels came from our custom world one, with NO_IR
+		 * on 5 GHz.  cfg80211 lifts that from beacon hints only while
+		 * world roaming, which a country IE ends: once associated, no
+		 * AP or GO could start on any 5 GHz channel, not even the
+		 * station's own.  Lift NO_IR where the country IE's rules
+		 * allow initiating radiation, as for world regulatory domains
+		 * (radar frequencies excepted).
+		 */
+		if (!ath_is_world_regd(reg))
+			ath_reg_apply_beaconing_flags(wiphy, reg,
+						      request->initiator);
+		else
+			ath_reg_dyn_country(wiphy, reg, request);
 		break;
 	}
 }
